**Why this and not relaxing the gate / not always-CAS:** The genuine first-publish branch must stay reachable because it performs the TEE enrollment (`encrypted_ipns_for_tee` + `key_epoch`, crypto rule #7) that `publish_with_cas_retry` does not send, and the strict gate requires the first publish to embed seq=1. The resolve guard preserves TEE enrollment for real new files while deterministically diverting any stale-hint re-publish onto CAS.

**Signature/threading:** none. `resolve_ipns_for_replay` is `pub(crate)` (`publish.rs:39`), `IpnsResolveOutcome` is `pub` (`error.rs:8`); both are already in-crate. `coordinator` and `api` are already in scope. No caller changes; `is_first_publish` stays in the signature (still the hint input).

**Scope:** Rust-only. No TS/bin helper changes. `pnpm api:generate` not needed (no API surface change).

### Local validation

- **Compile:** `cargo check -p cipherbox-fuse --features fuse` (macOS/Linux) — the `#[cfg(any(feature = "fuse", feature = "winfsp"))]` gate means the WinFsp variant is compile-checked only on the CI `Cargo Check & Test (Windows)` job (Windows is CI-only per project memory; budget a CI round-trip to confirm the shared function still builds under `winfsp`).
- **No unit coverage:** `publish_file_node` has no live-API unit test; `cargo test` will not exercise the equivocation. The authoritative check is the D-16 desktop-e2e leg `tests/desktop-e2e/scripts/shared-scope-exit-rotation.mts` (a `.mts` requiring the local stack: docker infra + `api dev` + a freshly built desktop mount with matching `TEST_LOGIN_SECRET`). Run it end-to-end and confirm no `Per-file node publish failed ... equivocation` in the mount log and that Part A still passes the single-rotation `+1` sequence-bump assertion. Note the ROADMAP still lists `70.1-13-PLAN.md` (the D-16 real-mount acceptance leg) as open — this fix is a prerequisite for that leg to go green.

